Subject: [EXPERIMENT] ASoC: accept the FullIO topology for the native Denali route

The topology gate was introduced for the separate silent fixture. The
native protected render route is also an explicitly selected Denali
fixture (DT `microsoft,denali-fullio-reference-render`) and must load
the same v19c graph. Everything else still rejects FullIO records.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c
@@ -1186,6 +1186,9 @@ static int audioreach_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 				   struct snd_soc_tplg_dapm_widget *tplg_w)
 {
-	bool muted_fixture = of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali") &&
-		of_property_read_bool(component->card->dev->of_node,
-				      "microsoft,denali-fullio-muted-test");
+	/* Explicit diagnostic or native fixtures may load the FullIO graph. */
+	bool muted_fixture = of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali") &&
+		(of_property_read_bool(component->card->dev->of_node,
+				      "microsoft,denali-fullio-muted-test") ||
+		 of_property_read_bool(component->card->dev->of_node,
+				      "microsoft,denali-fullio-reference-render"));
 	int ret = audioreach_validate_private(&tplg_w->priv, muted_fixture);
